# ---- param descriptions ----
mj2x.param.global.input.desc=Input file (.class / .jar)
mj2x.param.global.output.desc=Output file (.class / .jar; methods marked native)
mj2x.param.global.backend.desc=Select the native emission backend (stackc default; cbackend/c accepted as legacy aliases)
mj2x.param.global.emit_c.desc=Output C source path
mj2x.param.global.emit_cpp.desc=Output RegC C++17 source path (requires .cpp suffix + --backend regc)
mj2x.param.global.emit_llvm.desc=Output LLVM textual IR path (requires .ll suffix + --backend llvm)
mj2x.param.global.emit_native_dir.desc=RegC: multi-file output (mj2x_regc_api.h + runtime.c + per-class m_<Class>.c + entry.c)
mj2x.param.global.dump_mir.desc=Print the intermediate representation (debug)
mj2x.param.selection.native_annotation.desc=Translate only methods carrying the target annotation (JVM descriptor, e.g. Lmj2x/Native;)
mj2x.param.selection.native_method_prefixes.desc=Translate only methods whose owner.name starts with the given prefix (repeatable)
mj2x.param.compile.enabled.desc=Compile the generated C/C++ source into a native library (next to --output)
mj2x.param.compile.mode.desc=Native compilation input mode
mj2x.param.compile.opt_level.desc=Optimization level for the generated native project (0/1/2/3/s, default 2; lower levels keep source-level shapes such as CFF flattening from being optimized away, s targets size)
mj2x.param.compile.c_compiler.desc=C compiler or build driver (xmake = build driver)
mj2x.param.compile.llvm_tool.desc=LLVM IR compilation path
mj2x.param.compile.generate_cmake.desc=Generate a standalone CMake native project directory
mj2x.param.compile.generate_xmake.desc=Generate a standalone xmake native project directory (recommended; with --compile produces a DLL/SO in one step)
mj2x.param.stackc.exception_check.desc=StackC pending-exception check density (lite keeps only handler-boundary checks)
mj2x.param.regc.trace_calls.desc=RegC: emit runtime call logs ([CALL]/[DEEP] to stderr, for troubleshooting)
mj2x.param.regc.direct_calls.desc=RegC: enable native-to-native direct C calls (off by default: direct calls produce no JVM stack frames, breaking getStackTrace-like semantics)
mj2x.param.regc.comment_level.desc=RegC: generated comment level
mj2x.param.regc.safe_env.desc=RegC: enable safe-env (JNI function table snapshot + method entry restore; JNI_OnLoad fails closed if the table is already tainted at capture time)
mj2x.param.regc.safe_env_debug.desc=RegC: safe-env debug observation mode (detected hooks only warn instead of failing; implies --regc-safe-env)
mj2x.param.regc.no_inline.desc=RegC: disable SSA method inlining (on by default: semantics-equivalent inlining gated on static calls + no-exception regions + size/recursion, removing inter-method JNI round trips)
mj2x.param.regc.obfuscate.desc=RegC/LLVM: enable the base obfuscation transforms (MBA + opaque predicates + CFF flattening; RegIR-level, shared with RegC; all off by default keeping the fastest semantic-direct path; LLVM-side artifacts exceeding the subset fall back to untransformed)
mj2x.param.regc.cff_dead.desc=RegC/LLVM: CFF constant-false dead-block density (0 = off by default; N = 1 dead block per N jumps; the dead-block condition depends on runtime state, so the compiler cannot prove it constantly false and must not DCE; methods with injected barriers fall back to untransformed on the LLVM side)
mj2x.param.regc.cff_state_encrypt.desc=RegC/LLVM: CFF derived random state codes + dispatcher state XOR (off by default; same seed = same artifact)
mj2x.param.regc.mba_deep.desc=RegC: deep MBA (De Morgan/carry chains + anti-folding barriers, per-site variants; off by default; LLVM-side barriers exceed the subset, the transform falls back to untransformed)
mj2x.param.regc.opaque_zero.desc=RegC/LLVM: opaque-zero identity variants (demorgan/shift-pair/or-dec, variant chosen by seed; off by default)
mj2x.param.regc.transform_seed.desc=RegC/LLVM: transform seed (default 0; drives state codes/variant selection, same seed = same artifact)
mj2x.param.vmc4.dispatcher.desc=VMC4 (experimental): dispatcher form (switch_table default; computed_goto needs GCC/clang)
mj2x.param.vmc4.seed.desc=VMC4: master seed driving per-instance opcode mapping/handler order (same seed + same input = same artifact)
mj2x.param.vmc4.granularity.desc=VMC4: instance granularity (class default; method = one VM instance per method, strongest variability; program = one shared VM instance, smallest footprint)
mj2x.param.vmc4.alias.desc=VMC4: alias bytes per semantic ALT, 0..3 (0 = aliasing off)
mj2x.param.vmc4.bogus.desc=VMC4: number of injected unreachable fake handlers, 0..4 (0 = off; pollutes static analysis only, never executes)
mj2x.param.vmc4.drift.desc=VMC4: runtime dispatch variants, 0..4 (0 = off; when on, semantic labels rotate by byte-offset period, decoded via the unmap table)
mj2x.param.vmc4.drift_period.desc=VMC4: drift variant switch period (in byte offsets)
mj2x.param.vmc4.trace_surface.desc=VMC4: write the expected trace surface file (mjdbg red-team contract; same seed + same input = same content)
mj2x.param.vmc4.encrypt_program.desc=VMC4: encrypt the program blob at rest (opcode/handler data encrypted at emission, decrypted at interpreter load; no plaintext program stream in artifacts; key derived from seed; off by default)
mj2x.param.vmc4.lazy_decrypt.desc=VMC4: decrypt the program blob lazily per chunk (instruction-aligned 64-byte chunks encrypted independently, decrypted on first execution, key material scrubbed after use; requires vmc4.encrypt_program; off by default)
mj2x.param.vmc4.block_lazy_decrypt.desc=VMC4: decrypt the program blob lazily per CFG block (blocks bounded by the indirect jump table, chain keys derived as (seed, blockIdx, prevKey) with the first block keyed from the seed, decrypted on first arrival, unexecuted blocks stay encrypted, key material scrubbed after use; requires vmc4.encrypt_program, mutually exclusive with vmc4.lazy_decrypt; pairs with vmc4.shuffle-blocks; issue #1116 slice B; off by default)
mj2x.param.vmc4.shuffle_blocks.desc=VMC4: shuffle VM block layout at emission time (Sattolo single-cycle permutation over block ids and physical order, entry block fixed at id 0, control flow preserved via the encrypted indirect jump table; orthogonal and stackable with vmc4-drift and vmc4-encrypt-program; issue #1116 slice A; off by default)
mj2x.param.strings.encrypt.desc=Encrypt string-pool contents at rest (encrypted at emission, decrypted on first access; no plaintext literals in emitted artifacts; off by default)
mj2x.param.runtime.protection.desc=RegC/VMC4/LLVM: method-entry anti-tamper checkpoints (default none = not injected; depends on the mj2x-rt rt_protect module; the LLVM side compiles with rt_protect sources)
mj2x.param.runtime.protection_step.desc=Checkpoint probabilistic trigger step
mj2x.param.runtime.protection_delay_ms.desc=Delay action sleep in milliseconds
mj2x.param.native_lib.key.desc=Encrypted native lib storage: XOR-encrypt before embedding (xorshift32 keystream), .enc suffix on the resource entry, decrypted at load time by NativeLoader; a static extraction cannot be loaded directly (off by default = plaintext embedding)
mj2x.param.native_lib.pack_hook.desc=Pre-embedding external hook (e.g. sepacker DLL packing): the {in} placeholder is replaced with the built artifact path, the hook should rewrite the file in place; a non-zero exit is a failure; order: hook -> optional encryption -> embedding (off by default)
mj2x.param.client.id.desc=Per-client unique derivation (default 0 = unchanged: artifacts stay byte-identical to history; non-zero derives every backend seed via splitmix64(baseSeed ^ clientId), giving each client a unique ISA/variant/state-code artifact; same clientId + same seed = same artifact)
mj2x.param.intrinsic.config.desc=User-defined intrinsic JSON (issue #818): {"intrinsics":[{owner,name,desc,symbol,...}],"sources":[...]}
mj2x.param.intrinsic.sources.desc=Append user intrinsic implementation sources (repeatable; compiled into the generated project)
mj2x.param.log.quiet.desc=Keep only warnings and errors in the log (stderr)
mj2x.param.log.verbose.desc=Raise the log level to debug (stderr)
